Condition dataset notice
------------------------

``condition/orderly_condition.csv.gz`` is a normalized derivative of the
ORDerly-condition version 4 benchmark by Wigh et al. The source dataset and
normalized table are under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International.
Preserve attribution, the source DOI ``10.6084/m9.figshare.23298467.v4``, and
the article DOI ``10.1021/acs.jcim.4c00292``. SynRXN retains ORDerly's generic
agent roles and does not infer catalyst, ligand, base, or additive subclasses.

``condition/uspto_500.csv.gz`` is currently a byte-identical compatibility
mirror of ``synthesis/uspto_500.csv.gz``. It must not be counted as an
additional independent dataset or additional reaction records. The condition
path will become canonical in a later release phase.

Source license: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

``condition_sharealike/ord_hte_condition.csv.gz`` is a modified aggregate of sixteen
datasets from the Open Reaction Database. The ORD data repository explicitly
licenses datasets under ``data/`` and their metadata under Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International. SynRXN excludes the Pfizer 39k,
5,760-record Suzuki-Miyaura, Ahneman, and AstraZeneca 750 cohorts because those
source experiments already occur in the yield collection. Preserve ORD and
contributor attribution and distribute adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0.

``condition_sharealike/openexp.csv.gz`` is a modified table from the authors' exact
274,439-record ``OpenExp.tar`` OSF snapshot. Appendix A.1 of the ReactXT paper
states that OpenExp is released under CC BY-SA and requires the same license
for distribution and sharing. SynRXN retains the original procedure and action
sequence and adds a deterministic transformation-group split because the
released code's random 8:1:1 split has no fixed seed.

Both ShareAlike artifacts are distributed from the physically separate
``condition_sharealike/`` partition, which carries its own license text,
attribution notice, and manifest. They must never be redistributed inside an
archive whose notice omits the ShareAlike obligation.

ShareAlike source license: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
Full text: ``condition_sharealike/LICENSE`` (also ``sources/condition/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt``)


Yield dataset notices
---------------------

``yield/suzuki_miyaura.csv.gz`` is present only on the local ``yield`` branch
while written permission is pending. Its source is Perera et al., Science 2018,
DOI ``10.1126/science.aap9112``. No redistribution license has been verified;
``LicenseRef-Unknown`` grants no rights. Do not publish or include this file in
a release until the rights holder supplies written terms. The normalized
structure representations use mappings from ``rxn4chemistry/rxn_yields``.

``yield/buchwald_hartwig_ood.csv.gz`` is a modified, normalized table derived
from the BH-HTE-OOD repository snapshot identified in
``Data/sources/yield/buchwald_hartwig_ood.json``. It remains under Apache License
2.0. SynRXN removed 59 records whose reported yields exceeded the normalized
0--100 percent range and changed the source schema. A copy of Apache License
2.0 is distributed as ``Data/sources/yield/APACHE-2.0.txt``. Upstream source and
license: https://github.com/schwallergroup/bh-hte-ood

``yield/hitea.csv.gz`` is a modified, normalized table derived from the HiTEA
repository snapshot identified in ``Data/sources/yield/hitea.json``. It remains
under the following MIT terms:

